@startuml usdk_conversation
' Reconciles the task-supplied starting sequence sketch (user turn ->
' evidence/uncertainty -> loaded model driver produces a candidate ->
' three distinct role checks approve/reject -> approved text
' displayed/spoken -> permitted robotics action executes; rejected
' action never executes) with the actual call sequence as built - see
' packages/host-browser/src/index.mjs sendText()/proposeRoboticsAction()/
' _runRound(), and docs/UAGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md "Ensure external effects
' pass through the agreement gate" / "Prevention of stale speech".
'
' RENDERING UNVERIFIED: no local PlantUML CLI or plantuml.jar+Java found
' in this environment - see docs/diagrams/usdk_uagent_components.puml's
' header note; this .puml ships unrendered per the task's own
' instruction not to download tooling.

actor User
participant "uagent UI\n(app.mjs)" as UI
participant "ConversationSession\n(host-browser)" as Session
participant "perceive" as Perceive
participant "deliberate" as Deliberate
participant "Core\n(round state machine)" as Core
participant "verify" as Verify
participant "driver-voice /\ndriver-robotics-sim" as Driver

== Text turn - approved path ==

User -> UI : types message, submits
UI -> Session : sendText(text)
activate Session
Session -> Session : turnId = fresh id\n_currentTurnId = turnId
Session -> Perceive : observe(text, uncertainty=0.1)
Perceive --> Session : evidenceRef
Session -> Deliberate : propose(text, [evidenceRef])
Deliberate --> Session : responseText

alt _currentTurnId != turnId\n(a newer call or cancelTurn() superseded this one)
  Session --> UI : { status: 'superseded' }
else still current
  Session -> Session : createCandidate({..., evidenceRef,\nresponseText, constraint:\n"workspace:temp-only"})
  Session -> Core : openRound(candidate)
  Core --> Session : round

  Session -> Perceive : vote(candidate)
  Perceive --> Session : ACCEPT "evidence-verified"
  Session -> Core : submitVote(round, perceiveVote)

  Session -> Deliberate : vote(candidate)
  Deliberate --> Session : ACCEPT (self-consistency: matches propose() output)
  Session -> Core : submitVote(round, deliberateVote)

  Session -> Verify : vote(candidate)
  Verify --> Session : ACCEPT (evidence sufficient,\nconstraint permitted)
  Session -> Core : submitVote(round, verifyVote)

  Session -> Core : decide(round)
  activate Core
  note right of Core
    Commit rule: ACCEPT from ALL
    THREE roles required. REJECT,
    ABSTAIN, timeout, a detected
    candidate mutation, or a missing
    vote all prevent commit - see
    docs/CONSENSUS_PROTOCOL.md.
  end note
  Core -> Core : all three ACCEPT -> COMMITTED
  Core -> Driver : dispatchFn(candidate)\n(ONLY reached on commit)
  Driver --> Core : speak() onDone / n/a for text
  Core --> Session : state = COMMITTED
  deactivate Core

  Session -> Session : re-check _currentTurnId == turnId\n(guards against a cancellation that\narrived while decide() was running)
  Session -> UI : { status: 'committed', text: responseText }
end
UI -> User : displays approved text,\nannounces via aria-live
deactivate Session

== Robotics action - permitted path ==

User -> UI : clicks "Move forward"
UI -> Session : proposeRoboticsAction({direction, distanceM, speedMS})
Session -> Session : validateRoboticsAction(action)\n(fails fast if malformed - before\nany candidate/round exists)
Session -> Perceive : observe(actionJson, uncertainty=0.05)
Perceive --> Session : evidenceRef
Session -> Deliberate : proposeDirect(actionJson)
Session -> Session : createCandidate({..., constraint:\n"robotics:bounded-move"})
Session -> Core : openRound + 3x vote + decide (as above)
Core -> Driver : dispatchFn(candidate)\ndriver-robotics-sim.execute(action)
Driver -> Driver : re-validate bounds\n(independent of proposal-time check)
Driver --> Core : { completed: true/false }
Core --> Session : state = COMMITTED
Session -> Session : result.executionCompleted =\nlastDispatchResult.completed
Session --> UI : { status: 'committed',\nexecutionCompleted }
UI -> User : "Approved and executed" OR\n"Approved, but did not complete\n(stopped or interrupted)"

== Robotics action - rejected (never executes) ==

User -> UI : proposes an out-of-policy action
UI -> Session : proposeRoboticsAction(action)
Session -> Core : openRound + 3x vote\n(verify votes REJECT:\nconstraint not in allowedConstraints)
Core -> Core : not unanimous ACCEPT -> REJECTED
note right of Core
  dispatchFn is NEVER called on a
  non-committed round - this is
  enforced by Core.decide()'s own
  control flow, not by driver-side
  discretion.
end note
Core --> Session : state = REJECTED
Session --> UI : { status: 'rejected' }
UI -> User : "Not approved (rejected)"

== Emergency stop - bypasses deliberation entirely ==

User -> UI : clicks EMERGENCY STOP
UI -> Session : emergencyStop()
Session -> Driver : emergencyStop()\n(direct call, no round,\nno candidate, no vote)
Driver -> Driver : cancel in-progress\nsimulated movement immediately
note over Session, Driver
  A round already COMMITTED before
  the estop arrives can still report
  status: 'committed' (the PROPOSAL
  was approved) while
  executionCompleted: false (the
  movement itself did not finish) -
  these are different facts, both
  surfaced to the UI. Found via live
  interactive browser testing, not
  designed upfront - see
  docs/UAGENT_ARCHITECTURE.md
  "Robotics".
end note

@enduml
